"""Minimal reproducer: SA-3 equal-weight stagnation of the sweep-Schur CP response.

THE PHENOMENON (production): solve_state_sweep_schur stagnates at true relative
residual ~5e-2..1e-1 on SA-3 equal-weight systems (6m dithiocarbonate CAS(22,18),
def2-SVP) while every repo validation -- ALL of which is SA-2 -- certifies to 1e-6+.

THE HYPOTHESIS UNDER TEST (found by reading sweep_coupled_response.py):
_ci_block_inverse solves (H - E_i) v = w  per state (left_mpo = _hcc_shifted_mpo),
but the CI-CI block of the coupled operator (H_CC_apply_mps, and its dense twin
CPCASSCFResponseFCI.H_CC_apply / pyscf newton_casscf) is

        H_CC[i] = 2 * w_i * (H - E_i)   (+ SA-gauge rank-2 corrections).

The Schur elimination therefore uses an H_CC^{-1} that is wrong by the factor
1/(2 w_i).  For SA-2 equal weights 2*w = 1 exactly -- every existing test is
blind to it.  For SA-3 equal weights the factor is 2/3; for SA-5 it is 2/5.
The assembled solution then has an O(|1 - 2w|) *relative* true residual, which
no amount of proj_weight (S1), m_compress (S2) or inner-solve effort (S3) can
remove -- exactly the observed flat stagnation.

THE EXPERIMENT (H4 near-square rectangle, 3-21G, CAS(4,4), engineered
near-degeneracy; DMRG = FCI so the dense PySCF response is exactly solvable):

  A. dense EXACT solve: probe the full projected coupled Hessian (newton_casscf
     backend, pyscf project_Aop convention), solve exactly in the complement of
     the SA root space.  This is the certified answer.
  B. SA-2 control: sweep-Schur must certify (repo status quo).
  C. SA-3 with the CURRENT algebra (hcc_weight_scaling=False): measure the floor.
  D. SA-3 scans: proj_weight in {1e1,1e3,1e5,1e7}, m_compress/ci_m loop values,
     ci_sweeps -- the floor must NOT move if the weight factor is the disease.
  E. SA-3 with the FIX (hcc_weight_scaling=True, scale each block solve by
     1/(2 w_i)): must certify to <=1e-8 in true residual and match the dense z.
  F. dense REPLICA of the Schur algorithm (pure numpy, penalty + factor toggles):
     predicts the floor for each configuration with zero MPS noise, closing the
     mechanistic loop.

Run:  python test_sa3_equal_weight_response_reproducer.py [--stage quick|scan|all]
Writes JSON next to this file.
"""

